# Catch-all for a pipeline run written to a name not listed above
# (`agenthound local -o myscan.json`). Root-anchored, so the tracked JSON under
# schemas/, tests/fixtures/, examples/, and bloodhound/ is unaffected. A root
# JSON file that genuinely belongs in the repo can still be added with `git add -f`.
/*.json
# Local engagement scope files, host-specific, not part of the project.
scope.yaml

# Third-party tooling scratch and caches
.ua/

# Local-only working files, never published. Also listed in .git/info/exclude;
# duplicated here because that file is not committed and does not survive a
# fresh clone, so on its own the protection did not travel with the repository.
.planning/
local/
CLAUDE.md
.claude/
